---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
interface Props {
  kind: 'privacy' | 'support';
}
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const title =
  kind === 'privacy' ? 'SeamCarry Privacy Policy' : 'SeamCarry Support';
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} — Hailink Labs`}
  description="SeamCarry local sewing records, paper version checks, backups and purchase support."
>
  <section class="section intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Hailink Labs · SeamCarry</p>
    <h1>{title}</h1>
  </section>
  <article class="policy prose">
    <p>
      <a href="/products/seamcarry">About SeamCarry</a>
    </p>
    {kind === 'privacy' ? (
      <>
        <p>Effective October 7, 2026. SeamCarry 1.0.</p>
        <h2>Local records and photos</h2>
        <p>
          Patterns, changes, paper versions, make snapshots, notes and copied
          photos stay on your device. SeamCarry has no account, advertising,
          analytics, tracking, AI uploads or user-content server. Hailink Labs
          does not receive these records through the app.
        </p>
        <h2>Optional photo access</h2>
        <p>
          Photo selection uses the system picker. Camera permission is requested
          only when you choose Take Photo. You can continue with text if
          permission is declined. Imported photos are independent app copies;
          deleting the original from Photos does not remove the app copy.
        </p>
        <h2>Apple and chosen file providers</h2>
        <p>
          Apple processes purchases and restores through StoreKit. Verified
          access is stored locally; backups do not contain purchase credentials.
          You choose where to save PDF, CSV and complete backups and whom to
          share them with. Files providers handle transfers under their own
          policies. iCloud Drive is file backup, not automatic database
          synchronization. Complete backups may contain original photos and
          metadata. Protect them as private files; SeamCarry does not
          additionally encrypt backups.
        </p>
        <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Trash retains deleted patterns for at least 30 days until permanent
          deletion. Historical snapshots, backups and local recovery checkpoints
          may retain earlier records. You can edit, export and delete records.
          Uninstalling, losing or damaging the device may lose local data
          without an external backup. Restore Purchases restores access, not
          pattern data.
        </p>
        <h2>Website and support</h2>
        <p>
          This website uses GitHub Pages, which may process connection and
          request information under its own privacy statement. There are no
          website advertising, analytics, contact forms or tracking cookies.
          Voluntary support email and the information you choose to send are
          used to respond to your request, separately from local app records.
          Existing{' '}
          <a href="/products/samejob/privacy">
            company support correspondence practices
          </a>{' '}
          apply. Do not send private photos or full backups unless needed and
          intentionally shared.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">
            Apple Privacy Policy
          </a>{' '}
          ·{' '}
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
            GitHub Privacy Statement
          </a>
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <h2>Check your paper before cutting</h2>
        <p>
          Create a pattern and label the paper copy with its short code. Record
          changes as Needs check. After making a change on that copy, confirm
          Applied, or choose Not using with a reason. Confirm the paper label,
          view and size before sealing a version and before every new make.
          Ready records your confirmation; it does not certify fit or geometry.
          New versions copy notes but require fresh confirmations.
        </p>
        <h2>History and backups</h2>
        <p>
          Make snapshots preserve the version used. PDF and CSV are reports, not
          full-size sewing patterns or restorable backups. Create a complete
          .seamcarry backup in Settings and save it outside this device. Restore
          validates and previews the backup, creates a local checkpoint and
          replaces the full library. It does not merge libraries or transfer
          purchases. Keep a current external backup before restoring.
        </p>
        <h2>Two patterns free; optional Lifetime</h2>
        <p>
          Two patterns are free with every feature. Archived patterns count;
          Trash and the separate sample do not. The US Lifetime non-consumable
          purchase is US$9.99 for unlimited new patterns, with the current price
          shown by Apple. No subscription. Existing records remain available to
          view, edit, export and back up after refunds or temporary store
          errors. Restore Purchases uses your App Store account.
        </p>
        <h2>Saving and help</h2>
        <p>
          If saving fails, preserve your records, check available storage and
          retry. Do not uninstall or clear data to troubleshoot. Camera is
          optional; use the photo picker or text instead. Email support with the
          app version, action and exact error. Do not send private photos or
          full backups unless you choose to share them for support.
        </p>
      </>
    )}
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=SeamCarry%20Support`}>
        {site.email}
      </a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/products/seamcarry/support">Support</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/products/seamcarry/privacy">Privacy policy</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/contact">Contact Hailink Labs</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
